1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:04,838
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,136 --> 00:00:13,430
[Ivy] <i>How can I get what I want from her</i>

3
00:00:13,513 --> 00:00:15,265
<i>if she doesn't trust me?</i>

4
00:00:15,348 --> 00:00:17,726
<i>Trust can't be rushed, sweetie.</i>

5
00:00:17,809 --> 00:00:20,020
<i>But I know ways to gain it.</i>

6
00:00:20,103 --> 00:00:22,522
<i>Every person we let into our lives</i>

7
00:00:22,605 --> 00:00:25,316
<i>serves a purpose, Arnaldo.</i>

8
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:26,860
<i>It's better that at this point,</i>

9
00:00:26,943 --> 00:00:28,695
<i>you've already figured out</i>
<i>her purpose in your life.</i>

10
00:00:28,778 --> 00:00:30,488
[Ivy] <i>Starting today,</i>

11
00:00:30,572 --> 00:00:32,657
<i>I will befriend…</i>

12
00:00:32,741 --> 00:00:36,619
<i>Gov. Emilia Ardiente-Torillo.</i>

13
00:00:36,703 --> 00:00:40,957
<i>I guess Ms. Ivy's one</i>
<i>of the governor's friends now.</i>

14
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:43,126
<i>I must've had the wrong impression of her.</i>

15
00:00:43,209 --> 00:00:44,627
<i>So, why are you stalking me?</i>

16
00:00:44,711 --> 00:00:47,297
<i>Let's just say, to make it up to you.</i>

17
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:49,758
<i>Maybe I can help in your foundation.</i>

18
00:00:49,841 --> 00:00:51,718
<i>Natalie. I'm Arnaldo's girlfriend.</i>

19
00:00:51,801 --> 00:00:53,636
[Julio] <i>Natalie is your future.</i>

20
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:57,182
<i>And Ivy, she's nice</i>
<i>to have, but on the side.</i>

21
00:00:57,265 --> 00:00:59,184
[Carlotta] <i>You're looking</i>
<i>for justice, right?</i>

22
00:00:59,267 --> 00:01:02,103
<i>It'll take you a while</i>
<i>before you find evidence.</i>

23
00:01:02,187 --> 00:01:06,316
<i>But if you're after revenge,</i>
<i>it's as quick as one bullet.</i>

24
00:01:06,399 --> 00:01:08,693
<i>Hello? I have a job for you.</i>

25
00:01:08,777 --> 00:01:11,780
[man] <i>Emilia Ardiente-Torillo,</i>
<i>your days are over!</i>

26
00:01:12,113 --> 00:01:13,281
-[gunshot]
-[Ivy screams]

27
00:01:13,907 --> 00:01:15,450
<i>-Gov?!</i>
<i>-She saved me.</i>

28
00:01:15,533 --> 00:01:16,534
[Emilia] <i>She saved my life.</i>

29
00:01:16,618 --> 00:01:20,246
<i>I am the pillar of Ardiente!</i>
<i>Someone dared to go against me!</i>

30
00:01:20,538 --> 00:01:22,332
[Ivy] <i>Such a naughty boy, Mr. Mayor.</i>

31
00:01:22,707 --> 00:01:24,542
<i>Does your girlfriend know about you?</i>

32
00:01:24,626 --> 00:01:26,127
[Jepoy] <i>You weren't supposed</i>
<i>to hit anyone!</i>

33
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:27,629
[man] <i>I didn't expect her</i>
<i>to block the shot.</i>

34
00:01:27,712 --> 00:01:29,005
<i>They think you're dead now.</i>

35
00:01:29,088 --> 00:01:31,257
<i>So leave this town and never come back!</i>

36
00:01:34,427 --> 00:01:37,555
Our family is truly grateful
to you, Miss Aguas.

37
00:01:37,806 --> 00:01:39,516
We are forever indebted.

38
00:01:40,099 --> 00:01:42,811
You showed admirable courage.

39
00:01:45,021 --> 00:01:49,150
[groans] Congressman, I just did
what was right.

40
00:01:50,819 --> 00:01:52,195
You're an extraordinary woman.

41
00:01:56,324 --> 00:01:59,035
[Julio] Well, should you ever
need anything…

42
00:01:59,410 --> 00:02:00,495
just say so.

43
00:02:00,912 --> 00:02:03,623
This house is always open to you.

44
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:05,542
Stay for as long as you like.

45
00:02:05,875 --> 00:02:08,962
No, thank you. I wouldn't want to bother…

46
00:02:09,045 --> 00:02:11,464
I'll only be bothered

47
00:02:11,548 --> 00:02:14,634
if I let you go home
tonight in your condition.

48
00:02:15,468 --> 00:02:16,511
Stay here for the night.

49
00:02:17,137 --> 00:02:20,098
Please, allow us to take care of you.

50
00:02:20,974 --> 00:02:23,101
Just for tonight.

51
00:02:25,395 --> 00:02:26,896
Thank you, Congressman.

52
00:02:28,731 --> 00:02:31,442
If you'll excuse me, I have to go.

53
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:35,196
Emilia, please take care of Miss Aguas.

54
00:02:35,446 --> 00:02:36,447
Of course, Papa.

55
00:02:45,582 --> 00:02:46,332
[door closing]

56
00:02:46,958 --> 00:02:47,876
[Ivy groans]

57
00:02:52,672 --> 00:02:55,717
I don't know where to start.

58
00:03:04,851 --> 00:03:06,936
No one has ever done this for me.

59
00:03:09,522 --> 00:03:13,943
Well, no one that wasn't my bodyguard.

60
00:03:15,904 --> 00:03:18,740
Governor, like I said…

61
00:03:19,991 --> 00:03:22,035
I only did what was right.

62
00:03:30,335 --> 00:03:31,586
Thank you.

63
00:03:32,503 --> 00:03:34,380
I'll forever be indebted to you…

64
00:03:35,798 --> 00:03:37,884
for what you did for me.

65
00:03:40,762 --> 00:03:42,555
We're family now, Ivy.

66
00:03:43,806 --> 00:03:47,268
[sinister music playing]

67
00:03:54,776 --> 00:03:58,780
[tense music playing]

68
00:04:19,509 --> 00:04:20,510
[door opening]

69
00:04:21,427 --> 00:04:26,182
[tense music playing]

70
00:04:36,192 --> 00:04:37,026
[door opening]

71
00:04:45,368 --> 00:04:49,372
[tense music continues playing]

72
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:02,677
[phone vibrating]

73
00:05:04,178 --> 00:05:05,638
[phone vibrating]

74
00:05:08,308 --> 00:05:10,393
-Nanny Carlotta.
-Ivy!

75
00:05:10,476 --> 00:05:12,103
[gasps] Ivy, I've been trying to call you.

76
00:05:12,186 --> 00:05:13,604
Why weren't you answering?

77
00:05:14,355 --> 00:05:16,107
I fell asleep.

78
00:05:16,649 --> 00:05:19,610
The governor sent someone
here to get your clothes.

79
00:05:20,236 --> 00:05:23,448
-<i>What happened?</i>
-I was shot.

80
00:05:23,865 --> 00:05:24,866
What?!

81
00:05:25,783 --> 00:05:27,660
The bullet just grazed me, though.

82
00:05:27,744 --> 00:05:29,787
<i>I'll tell you everything soon.</i>

83
00:05:29,996 --> 00:05:31,622
What's important is that I'm here now.

84
00:05:31,873 --> 00:05:33,249
Ivy!

85
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:35,877
Do you think you're still
going to find anything there?

86
00:05:36,419 --> 00:05:40,173
With how many years have
passed, it's near impossible.

87
00:05:41,007 --> 00:05:41,841
[sighs]

88
00:05:42,884 --> 00:05:45,845
I have to try first, Nanny Carlotta.

89
00:05:45,928 --> 00:05:49,348
-But it's dangerous, Ivy.
-<i>Nanny Carlotta…</i>

90
00:05:49,807 --> 00:05:51,184
When I came back here,

91
00:05:51,267 --> 00:05:54,520
I prepared myself for
the danger I'd be facing.

92
00:05:55,938 --> 00:05:57,148
<i>I'll talk to you later.</i>

93
00:05:57,231 --> 00:05:59,776
-Wait for me to come back.
-Ivy, wait--

94
00:06:00,777 --> 00:06:04,781
[tense music playing]

95
00:06:29,806 --> 00:06:33,810
[instrumental theme music playing]

96
00:07:03,506 --> 00:07:04,507
[door opening]

97
00:07:06,259 --> 00:07:10,054
-Nanny.
-Diego? Where are you going?

98
00:07:10,221 --> 00:07:11,264
Back home.

99
00:07:11,764 --> 00:07:14,016
Why don't you leave tomorrow morning?

100
00:07:14,434 --> 00:07:15,768
It's already late.

101
00:07:16,269 --> 00:07:18,062
Something's bothering me.

102
00:07:19,522 --> 00:07:22,692
If I don't go home
I won't be able to rest easy.

103
00:07:23,860 --> 00:07:25,945
-But--
-I'll be careful.

104
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:28,656
Just go to sleep, okay?

105
00:07:30,241 --> 00:07:31,909
-Take care.
-I will.

106
00:07:42,879 --> 00:07:45,673
[tense music playing]

107
00:08:04,567 --> 00:08:07,612
[music intensifies]

108
00:08:08,571 --> 00:08:09,322
[car locking]

109
00:08:34,639 --> 00:08:35,389
[door closing]

110
00:08:53,491 --> 00:08:57,495
[action music playing]

111
00:09:07,547 --> 00:09:08,923
[door opening]

112
00:09:15,805 --> 00:09:18,599
Where have you been?
Are you really that numb?

113
00:09:18,683 --> 00:09:20,851
I almost died, and you still don't care?

114
00:09:20,935 --> 00:09:22,520
Emilia, can we not do this? I'm tired.

115
00:09:22,603 --> 00:09:23,980
I asked you a question!

116
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:26,649
Where have you been?!

117
00:09:26,732 --> 00:09:28,317
-Didn't you hear me?
-[objects shatter]

118
00:09:28,651 --> 00:09:30,736
-Where'd you go?
-Are you deaf?

119
00:09:30,945 --> 00:09:32,697
I said I was tired from the trip!

120
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:34,365
So stop asking questions!

121
00:09:34,448 --> 00:09:36,826
-How dare you!
-Stop it.

122
00:09:41,581 --> 00:09:43,916
[Emilia] I can't ask? Huh? I can't?

123
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,168
[Raul] Stop it! I'm not in
the mood for this.

124
00:09:46,836 --> 00:09:49,463
Here's what you can do.
Why don't you just kill me…

125
00:09:49,797 --> 00:09:52,174
to solve all your problems?
I'm dead to you, remember?

126
00:09:52,925 --> 00:09:55,636
-After all this, huh?!
-Let go of me!

127
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:57,513
[Emilia] After all I've done for you!

128
00:09:57,597 --> 00:09:59,974
Till now you still don't understand

129
00:10:00,057 --> 00:10:02,351
why I did what I did for you!

130
00:10:02,435 --> 00:10:03,769
You don't understand!

131
00:10:03,853 --> 00:10:06,022
That I did everything because I love you!

132
00:10:07,064 --> 00:10:10,151
I became a murderer
because of my love for you!

133
00:10:11,986 --> 00:10:15,448
I promised myself I'd stop
killing because of you.

134
00:10:15,615 --> 00:10:18,701
But you're making things difficult for me!

135
00:10:19,035 --> 00:10:20,870
All you've ever done is remind me

136
00:10:20,953 --> 00:10:23,205
why I shouldn't regret finishing them off!

137
00:10:24,915 --> 00:10:26,792
Who are you fooling, Emilia?

138
00:10:27,793 --> 00:10:32,089
Just admit that you enjoyed
getting rid of them!

139
00:10:32,340 --> 00:10:34,800
That you enjoyed murdering those people!

140
00:10:34,967 --> 00:10:36,218
You're heartless.

141
00:10:36,636 --> 00:10:39,138
You even wiped out an entire family!

142
00:10:39,513 --> 00:10:40,556
[suspenseful sting]

143
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:44,310
You had to involve an innocent child, too!

144
00:10:44,393 --> 00:10:47,688
You didn't think how that affected Diego.

145
00:10:48,314 --> 00:10:49,982
You killed his best friend!

146
00:10:51,442 --> 00:10:53,069
[Emilia] After 13 years?

147
00:10:53,152 --> 00:10:55,029
-After 13 years, Raul…
-Yes.

148
00:10:55,112 --> 00:10:56,280
And we're still fighting about this?

149
00:10:56,364 --> 00:10:59,283
-Yes!
-Was it my fault?! Was it mine?!

150
00:10:59,367 --> 00:11:01,911
-Didn't you start all this?!
-Me?

151
00:11:01,994 --> 00:11:04,121
If only you didn't take
a liking to that girl's mother,

152
00:11:04,205 --> 00:11:05,915
then none of this would've happened!

153
00:11:05,998 --> 00:11:08,834
Her father wouldn't have gone against us!

154
00:11:08,918 --> 00:11:11,253
Did you think that girl wouldn't know?

155
00:11:11,337 --> 00:11:12,505
That she wouldn't accuse me?!

156
00:11:12,713 --> 00:11:15,174
It's just a choice between her and me!

157
00:11:15,758 --> 00:11:18,677
What if she ruins our family?
I won't allow her to!

158
00:11:18,761 --> 00:11:20,805
That's why it's good
they're all done with!

159
00:11:21,472 --> 00:11:22,890
I will kill anyone

160
00:11:22,973 --> 00:11:25,768
who dares ruin the family I've supported

161
00:11:25,851 --> 00:11:27,603
and everything we've worked for!

162
00:11:27,686 --> 00:11:29,271
I won't allow it!

163
00:11:29,563 --> 00:11:32,483
And I've done all this because I love you!

164
00:11:35,194 --> 00:11:38,114
Why can't you stop being unfaithful?

165
00:11:42,701 --> 00:11:44,453
Is that too much to ask?

166
00:11:45,162 --> 00:11:48,082
For you to love me? Is it so hard?

167
00:11:51,877 --> 00:11:54,880
How can I love a murderer like you?

168
00:11:59,427 --> 00:12:00,761
What? Go on!

169
00:12:00,845 --> 00:12:02,263
[Raul] Does the truth hurt?

170
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:04,765
[Emilia wails]

171
00:12:06,475 --> 00:12:08,060
You've killed so many people.

172
00:12:08,144 --> 00:12:09,812
Now, I'm going to kill you.

173
00:12:09,895 --> 00:12:11,814
I can kill you, too, Raul.

174
00:12:12,606 --> 00:12:14,817
-Not if I kill you first!
-You bastard!

175
00:12:14,942 --> 00:12:16,569
-I hate you!
-You piece of trash!

176
00:12:16,652 --> 00:12:17,486
Murderer!

177
00:12:17,570 --> 00:12:18,863
-Monster!
-Let go

178
00:12:18,946 --> 00:12:21,490
-I'll kill you!
-I'll kill you first!

179
00:12:22,992 --> 00:12:24,952
[Raul] I'll kill you first!
Do you understand?!

180
00:12:25,035 --> 00:12:26,704
-You bastard!
-Dad!

181
00:12:26,787 --> 00:12:29,123
-Dad, stop!
-[Emilia grunts]

182
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:31,167
[Raul] Murderer.

183
00:12:33,836 --> 00:12:34,753
Dad, what's going on?

184
00:12:36,422 --> 00:12:39,675
Dad, stop this. Whatever Mom's fault is,

185
00:12:40,134 --> 00:12:41,635
you don't have the right to hurt her.

186
00:12:44,305 --> 00:12:45,806
[Raul] Fine, side with her.

187
00:12:46,974 --> 00:12:50,853
I don't even understand why
I still come home to this house.

188
00:12:51,145 --> 00:12:53,522
We both know why!

189
00:12:54,356 --> 00:12:58,110
Because you want even a little
of the power the Ardientes have.

190
00:12:58,444 --> 00:13:00,821
But you will never be an Ardiente!

191
00:13:01,113 --> 00:13:02,615
You're just a leech!

192
00:13:02,698 --> 00:13:04,366
-A leech!
-Mom, stop.

193
00:13:04,450 --> 00:13:06,202
-You're not going to stop, are you?
-You leech!

194
00:13:06,285 --> 00:13:08,412
-Dad, stop.
-You just can't shut up, huh?

195
00:13:08,496 --> 00:13:11,290
-Come here.
-Dad, please, stop this.

196
00:13:11,582 --> 00:13:12,583
Let go of me.

197
00:13:12,958 --> 00:13:14,460
We're not done yet, Emilia.

198
00:13:19,632 --> 00:13:23,010
[tense music playing]

199
00:13:33,771 --> 00:13:35,773
-Mom?
-[Emilia weeps]

200
00:13:47,409 --> 00:13:48,410
Mom, don't cry.

201
00:13:55,793 --> 00:13:57,586
Emilia, you murderer.

202
00:13:58,504 --> 00:13:59,588
You murderer.

203
00:13:59,672 --> 00:14:00,589
<i>-Didn't you…</i>
<i>-Me?</i>

204
00:14:00,673 --> 00:14:02,174
[Emilia] <i>…start all this?!</i>

205
00:14:02,258 --> 00:14:04,552
<i>If only you didn't take</i>
<i>a liking to that girl's mother,</i>

206
00:14:04,635 --> 00:14:07,638
<i>her father wouldn't have gone against us.</i>

207
00:14:07,721 --> 00:14:09,765
You bitch. You monster.

208
00:14:09,848 --> 00:14:12,142
[Raul] <i>You enjoyed murdering those people.</i>

209
00:14:12,226 --> 00:14:14,937
<i>You wiped out an entire family!</i>

210
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:16,105
<i>You didn't think</i>

211
00:14:16,188 --> 00:14:18,315
<i>-how that affected Diego.</i>
-[gunshot]

212
00:14:18,399 --> 00:14:20,317
<i>You killed his best friend!</i>

213
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:24,196
You're all monsters.

214
00:14:24,905 --> 00:14:25,906
All of you.

215
00:14:28,659 --> 00:14:30,369
[tires screeching]

216
00:14:43,424 --> 00:14:44,341
What's your problem?!

217
00:14:44,425 --> 00:14:45,509
-You're my problem!
-What?!

218
00:14:45,593 --> 00:14:47,011
-You're my problem!
-Were you going to kill me?

219
00:14:47,094 --> 00:14:49,513
-Run me off the road?! Kill me, too?
-What did you want me to do?!

220
00:14:49,597 --> 00:14:50,347
You were driving so fast!

221
00:14:50,431 --> 00:14:51,432
-Monsters!
-Ivy.

222
00:14:51,515 --> 00:14:53,893
They're all monsters!

223
00:14:53,976 --> 00:14:54,935
Murderers!

224
00:14:55,019 --> 00:14:58,272
The Ardientes are all monsters!

225
00:14:59,648 --> 00:15:02,026
-Calm down. Calm down.
-[Ivy sobbing]

226
00:15:15,497 --> 00:15:17,333
They're monsters.

227
00:15:17,416 --> 00:15:20,669
Damn you, Emilia!

228
00:15:21,253 --> 00:15:26,050
The Ardientes should all burn in hell!

229
00:15:26,133 --> 00:15:31,096
[weeping]

230
00:15:40,689 --> 00:15:42,149
Calm down.

231
00:16:02,795 --> 00:16:04,797
[Carlotta] Have some water, dear.

232
00:16:06,632 --> 00:16:07,675
Please, Ivy.

233
00:16:07,883 --> 00:16:11,679
[somber music playing]

234
00:16:23,190 --> 00:16:25,442
I knew it, Nanny Carlotta.

235
00:16:29,029 --> 00:16:30,823
I knew she was the mastermind.

236
00:16:33,075 --> 00:16:35,119
But it's different…

237
00:16:38,706 --> 00:16:41,667
hearing her say that…

238
00:16:42,418 --> 00:16:44,628
she had my father killed.

239
00:16:47,881 --> 00:16:49,800
And my mother, too.

240
00:16:55,806 --> 00:16:58,726
I thought I already knew
that family enough…

241
00:16:59,601 --> 00:17:02,021
because of the documents you sent me.

242
00:17:03,981 --> 00:17:04,982
But…

243
00:17:07,317 --> 00:17:08,485
I was wrong.

244
00:17:14,408 --> 00:17:16,952
Whenever I see them…

245
00:17:18,579 --> 00:17:19,705
I can't help but remember

246
00:17:19,788 --> 00:17:23,459
what they did to my parents.

247
00:17:27,504 --> 00:17:28,839
Don't worry, Ivy.

248
00:17:31,633 --> 00:17:33,802
We'll locate where your mother is buried.

249
00:17:35,137 --> 00:17:38,557
I already found the hit man Emilia hired.

250
00:17:39,975 --> 00:17:40,976
He's alive.

251
00:17:42,519 --> 00:17:43,979
[Jepoy] You'll avenge your mother.

252
00:17:44,688 --> 00:17:45,898
Just give me some time.

253
00:18:00,287 --> 00:18:05,292
[somber music playing]

254
00:18:36,281 --> 00:18:41,286
[somber music continues playing]

255
00:19:09,606 --> 00:19:14,611
[sentimental music playing]

256
00:19:24,663 --> 00:19:26,206
-[young Lily] <i>Hey, let go of me!</i>
<i>-Come on.</i>

257
00:19:26,290 --> 00:19:29,251
<i>-Let go of me!</i>
-[whistles]

258
00:19:29,334 --> 00:19:30,878
<i>If you're in trouble, blow this.</i>

259
00:19:30,961 --> 00:19:32,921
<i>I'm the parking boy! Jepoy.</i>

260
00:19:36,466 --> 00:19:38,969
[Berto] <i>You think you're tough? Hit here!</i>

261
00:19:39,761 --> 00:19:40,804
<i>-He thinks he's tough!</i>
-[whistles]

262
00:19:40,888 --> 00:19:42,681
<i>The cops! Run!</i>

263
00:19:43,473 --> 00:19:44,808
[police officer]
<i>You two, chase after them!</i>

264
00:19:44,892 --> 00:19:47,603
<i>Stand up! Are you hurt?</i>

265
00:19:58,739 --> 00:20:00,949
<i>-Here, eat up.</i>
<i>-You know what?</i>

266
00:20:02,201 --> 00:20:04,870
<i>I thought I was done for</i>

267
00:20:04,953 --> 00:20:08,540
<i>because of Berto or the cops.</i>

268
00:20:08,624 --> 00:20:12,127
<i>Plus, I was starving!</i>
<i>You're like an angel.</i>

269
00:20:12,628 --> 00:20:14,004
<i>Don't mention it.</i>

270
00:20:14,421 --> 00:20:16,715
<i>Ms. Prianka and I</i>
<i>were supposed to head somewhere,</i>

271
00:20:16,798 --> 00:20:19,885
<i>but then we saw you getting beaten up.</i>

272
00:20:20,677 --> 00:20:21,720
<i>I just spoke to her,</i>

273
00:20:21,803 --> 00:20:23,931
<i>and she'll help you</i>
<i>and pay for your education.</i>

274
00:20:24,514 --> 00:20:27,434
<i>She said you can stay</i>
<i>at her house in the province.</i>

275
00:20:27,768 --> 00:20:28,810
<i>That's okay, right?</i>

276
00:20:29,770 --> 00:20:32,022
<i>Right? Hey!</i>

277
00:20:33,357 --> 00:20:34,775
<i>Hey! </i>[giggles]

278
00:20:35,275 --> 00:20:37,069
<i>Hey, that's fine, right?</i>

279
00:20:38,070 --> 00:20:43,367
[sentimental music playing]

280
00:20:43,450 --> 00:20:45,118
[no audible dialogue]

281
00:20:50,415 --> 00:20:51,583
<i>This is Madrigal.</i>

282
00:20:51,667 --> 00:20:54,670
<i>My most trusted man. He'll accompany us.</i>

283
00:20:56,964 --> 00:20:58,924
-[gunshot]
-[Emilia screams]

284
00:21:01,176 --> 00:21:03,011
[screaming] <i>Were you</i>
<i>going to kill me, too?</i>

285
00:21:04,805 --> 00:21:05,889
<i>Calm down.</i>

286
00:21:09,184 --> 00:21:12,771
[sentimental music continues playing]

287
00:21:17,526 --> 00:21:18,819
<i>I'll protect you.</i>

288
00:21:19,569 --> 00:21:22,114
<i>I'll never leave your side.</i>

289
00:21:24,241 --> 00:21:27,786
<i>Whatever happens, I won't leave you.</i>

290
00:21:36,753 --> 00:21:39,756
[somber music playing]

291
00:21:46,596 --> 00:21:47,597
[exhales sharply]

292
00:22:23,091 --> 00:22:25,052
Hey, Jepoy, where's Ivy?

293
00:22:25,719 --> 00:22:27,220
She's still sleeping in her room.

294
00:22:27,804 --> 00:22:28,805
Ah…

295
00:22:29,097 --> 00:22:31,058
-Uh, Nanny Carlotta.
-Yes?

296
00:22:31,767 --> 00:22:33,977
I'll set up security cameras around, okay?

297
00:22:34,061 --> 00:22:36,021
And add locks on the doors.

298
00:22:36,772 --> 00:22:38,607
It's too easy to break into this house.

299
00:22:39,441 --> 00:22:40,442
Jepoy…

300
00:22:41,109 --> 00:22:45,155
I know the two of us are here
because we both love her.

301
00:22:46,531 --> 00:22:48,075
So, please…

302
00:22:48,992 --> 00:22:50,660
take care of Ivy.

303
00:22:51,745 --> 00:22:54,289
Let's hope nothing bad happens to her.

304
00:22:54,372 --> 00:22:57,125
Nanny Carlotta, you don't have
to tell me that.

305
00:22:57,793 --> 00:23:00,378
You know I owe Ivy my life, right?

306
00:23:02,464 --> 00:23:06,676
I'll do everything and anything for her.

307
00:23:07,552 --> 00:23:08,345
Thank you.

308
00:23:21,817 --> 00:23:23,568
-[knocking on door]
-[door opening]

309
00:23:23,944 --> 00:23:26,530
Ivy, good--

310
00:23:48,468 --> 00:23:51,096
Did Ivy leave? Without saying goodbye?

311
00:23:52,097 --> 00:23:53,557
It seems she left last night, Papa.

312
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:55,308
But Arnaldo will call her.

313
00:23:58,061 --> 00:23:59,229
By the way, give me a copy

314
00:23:59,312 --> 00:24:01,481
of the information we got about her.

315
00:24:02,149 --> 00:24:07,279
I want to see how many
properties and assets she owns.

316
00:24:07,571 --> 00:24:10,532
I want to know just how much

317
00:24:10,615 --> 00:24:13,285
she can contribute to the Ardientes.

318
00:24:13,910 --> 00:24:14,911
Yes, Papa.

319
00:24:16,872 --> 00:24:17,622
Now.

320
00:24:26,131 --> 00:24:28,091
Have some coffee, dear.

321
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:32,929
Jepoy, come eat!

322
00:24:36,474 --> 00:24:37,559
[Carlotta] Take a seat.

323
00:24:39,603 --> 00:24:43,607
[tense music playing]

324
00:24:50,989 --> 00:24:53,491
Ivy, how's your wound?

325
00:25:01,875 --> 00:25:02,959
I know…

326
00:25:04,336 --> 00:25:06,838
Don't worry. It won't happen again.

327
00:25:16,765 --> 00:25:19,643
-Jepoy, have some bread.
-Thank you.

328
00:25:24,689 --> 00:25:25,440
You know what?

329
00:25:26,858 --> 00:25:28,151
The old man's biding his time.

330
00:25:29,110 --> 00:25:31,321
I'm sure he hasn't forgotten

331
00:25:31,404 --> 00:25:32,989
about the shooting attempt on Emilia.

332
00:25:35,283 --> 00:25:36,743
You need to lie low, Ivy.

333
00:25:39,329 --> 00:25:41,790
Divert their attention
while I look for your mother.

334
00:25:47,504 --> 00:25:49,506
[tense music playing]

335
00:26:01,768 --> 00:26:03,478
Let me, Ivy. Here's some toast.

336
00:26:05,897 --> 00:26:09,150
[sinister music playing]

337
00:26:09,234 --> 00:26:10,235
[Julio] Hmm…

338
00:26:17,826 --> 00:26:19,244
Oh. [chuckles]

339
00:26:19,327 --> 00:26:20,662
NET WORTH: 1.54 BILLION USD

340
00:26:21,037 --> 00:26:24,541
This can be an ace up my sleeve.

341
00:26:25,959 --> 00:26:27,335
All her wealth…

342
00:26:28,420 --> 00:26:31,381
Make sure we'll get all of it, Emilia.

343
00:26:32,132 --> 00:26:33,008
Yes, Papa.

344
00:26:34,676 --> 00:26:35,593
Hmm.

345
00:26:35,677 --> 00:26:36,720
You can eat now.

346
00:26:43,935 --> 00:26:45,103
[laughs viciously]

347
00:26:50,775 --> 00:26:53,987
NATIONAL CRIMINAL BACKGROUND CHECK

348
00:26:55,989 --> 00:26:58,533
[sinister music playing]

349
00:27:01,786 --> 00:27:03,204
[Jepoy] <i>You need to lie low, Ivy.</i>

350
00:27:03,496 --> 00:27:06,249
<i>Divert their attention</i>
<i>while I look for your mother.</i>

351
00:27:13,923 --> 00:27:14,924
[line ringing]

352
00:27:15,383 --> 00:27:17,218
-[phone ringing]
-You left your phone, dear.

353
00:27:17,302 --> 00:27:20,347
-Arnaldo is calling you.
-[phone ringing]

354
00:27:20,430 --> 00:27:21,431
Thank you.

355
00:27:22,807 --> 00:27:24,726
-[phone ringing]
-Mr. Mayor?

356
00:27:25,101 --> 00:27:26,644
You left without saying goodbye.

357
00:27:29,856 --> 00:27:32,275
Your family has done so much for me.

358
00:27:32,567 --> 00:27:35,445
I didn't want to overstay my welcome.

359
00:27:36,821 --> 00:27:38,656
[Arnaldo] <i>What are you talking about?</i>

360
00:27:38,740 --> 00:27:40,450
We're the ones who are indebted to you.

361
00:27:42,619 --> 00:27:44,496
Mr. Mayor, did you call for a reason,

362
00:27:44,579 --> 00:27:49,000
or did you just want to hear my voice?

363
00:27:49,584 --> 00:27:51,044
Uh, well…

364
00:27:51,294 --> 00:27:53,713
I wanted to invite you to breakfast.

365
00:27:53,797 --> 00:27:56,758
<i>I made you breakfast in bed. And also…</i>

366
00:27:57,342 --> 00:28:00,261
I want to talk to you about
the export processing zone.

367
00:28:00,887 --> 00:28:03,681
To make your family
even more indebted to me?

368
00:28:05,725 --> 00:28:06,726
Ah…

369
00:28:07,102 --> 00:28:08,603
-[chuckles]
-[scoffs]

370
00:28:09,020 --> 00:28:13,441
Mr. Mayor, why do I feel
like I made you blush?

371
00:28:13,525 --> 00:28:14,692
[chuckles]

372
00:28:15,151 --> 00:28:16,236
I was just kidding.

373
00:28:17,404 --> 00:28:19,072
Consider my investment done.

374
00:28:19,989 --> 00:28:20,740
Really?

375
00:28:22,492 --> 00:28:25,495
Like what your mother, the governor, said,

376
00:28:26,162 --> 00:28:27,914
we're family now.

377
00:28:28,915 --> 00:28:30,041
Wow. Wow.

378
00:28:30,125 --> 00:28:32,335
I… I don't know what to say.

379
00:28:38,508 --> 00:28:41,803
Are we clear about my plans, Mr. Fernan?

380
00:28:43,680 --> 00:28:45,390
I'll try to convince them.

381
00:28:46,891 --> 00:28:47,809
Mr. Fernan…

382
00:28:48,768 --> 00:28:51,354
You know that this will
benefit the entire town.

383
00:28:51,771 --> 00:28:53,565
It'll improve everyone's lives.

384
00:28:53,857 --> 00:28:57,026
The investors are ready
for this project, Mr. Fernan.

385
00:28:59,195 --> 00:29:01,322
But, Mayor, many people
will lose their land.

386
00:29:01,406 --> 00:29:03,867
Of course we have to make sacrifices.

387
00:29:04,075 --> 00:29:06,327
But it's for…

388
00:29:06,703 --> 00:29:08,788
the prosperity of everyone in this town.

389
00:29:08,872 --> 00:29:09,664
[scoffs]

390
00:29:09,748 --> 00:29:11,958
You're the first person I notified

391
00:29:12,041 --> 00:29:14,335
because you are the
president of the cooperative.

392
00:29:15,378 --> 00:29:18,173
[Arnaldo] I know you're capable
of understanding this project,

393
00:29:18,256 --> 00:29:19,507
for the whole town.

394
00:29:19,883 --> 00:29:22,510
Because, just like me,
you're a leader, too.

395
00:29:25,263 --> 00:29:26,765
Can I count on you, Mr. Fernan?

396
00:29:28,975 --> 00:29:29,726
[sighs]

397
00:29:39,486 --> 00:29:42,405
[Pandoy] Come on, Fernan.
It's not that simple!

398
00:29:42,697 --> 00:29:45,992
The cooperative will lose all the land!

399
00:29:46,075 --> 00:29:47,619
Is that what you're trying to say?!

400
00:29:48,286 --> 00:29:51,831
That's what we call "sacrifice," Pandoy!

401
00:29:51,915 --> 00:29:52,999
[slams table] Hold it!

402
00:29:53,208 --> 00:29:56,044
-Why do we have to sacrifice?
-That's right!

403
00:29:56,127 --> 00:29:57,879
Did the mayor sacrifice anything for us?

404
00:29:57,962 --> 00:30:00,840
-That's right!
-You don't get it.

405
00:30:00,924 --> 00:30:03,092
We will all benefit

406
00:30:03,176 --> 00:30:05,136
from the export processing zone!

407
00:30:05,220 --> 00:30:06,596
How? Tell us, how?!

408
00:30:06,679 --> 00:30:07,847
[Fernan] We're going to get jobs!

409
00:30:07,931 --> 00:30:10,016
[Loring] It's not that simple, Fernan!

410
00:30:10,099 --> 00:30:11,518
We have jobs!

411
00:30:11,601 --> 00:30:12,894
[Fernan] They're not
going to take our land!

412
00:30:12,977 --> 00:30:15,396
We need to expand our
understanding, and not just…

413
00:30:15,480 --> 00:30:16,815
-…get stuck farming.
-What are you saying?

414
00:30:16,898 --> 00:30:18,817
-That we're narrow-minded?!
-Yes!

415
00:30:18,900 --> 00:30:20,485
[Fernan] We have to widen our perspective!

416
00:30:20,568 --> 00:30:22,946
[Pandoy] Can you even
hear what you're saying?!

417
00:30:23,279 --> 00:30:24,572
What's happening here?

418
00:30:26,032 --> 00:30:27,283
It's the mayor.

419
00:30:27,492 --> 00:30:31,412
He wants to build an export zone here,

420
00:30:31,496 --> 00:30:33,873
on the land owned by the cooperative!

421
00:30:34,624 --> 00:30:38,169
Your brother's acting
like a greedy Ardiente again!

422
00:30:39,212 --> 00:30:42,549
And that Ivy, the woman who visited us?

423
00:30:43,466 --> 00:30:46,302
She's one of them! She's an investor!

424
00:30:46,386 --> 00:30:47,887
-That's right.
-Hey, wait.

425
00:30:48,388 --> 00:30:50,181
You're getting too personal, Loring.

426
00:30:50,515 --> 00:30:54,602
The Ardientes have been working
so hard to improve our lives!

427
00:30:54,686 --> 00:30:56,479
Right? Diego's proof of that!

428
00:30:56,563 --> 00:30:57,480
-There.
-Diego.

429
00:30:57,564 --> 00:31:01,985
And you proved that you don't
understand the situation

430
00:31:02,068 --> 00:31:04,070
-of the rest of us!
-But this is…

431
00:31:04,153 --> 00:31:05,321
Hold up. Hold up.

432
00:31:05,530 --> 00:31:07,156
-…all for us.
-Hold up. Hold up.

433
00:31:07,240 --> 00:31:08,241
Everyone, calm down.

434
00:31:08,741 --> 00:31:10,159
Let's stop arguing.

435
00:31:10,785 --> 00:31:12,245
You'll keep your land.

436
00:31:12,912 --> 00:31:14,122
I assure you.

437
00:31:14,706 --> 00:31:16,416
-We hope so.
-That's where we get our crops.

438
00:31:16,499 --> 00:31:17,876
-It's all we have.
-I hope…

439
00:31:17,959 --> 00:31:19,627
We hope you can help us, Diego.

440
00:31:19,711 --> 00:31:22,171
[woman] We've stayed here for so long.

441
00:31:22,255 --> 00:31:24,841
-We can't get another job.
-What about our kids?

442
00:31:24,924 --> 00:31:25,967
I'll take care of this.

443
00:31:30,763 --> 00:31:33,892
They're willing to let go
of their land, just like that?

444
00:31:35,310 --> 00:31:36,060
[chuckles]

445
00:31:37,270 --> 00:31:38,980
Ms. Aguas…

446
00:31:39,063 --> 00:31:41,816
are you doubting my
ability to convince people?

447
00:31:44,485 --> 00:31:45,445
As long as you assure me,

448
00:31:45,528 --> 00:31:48,990
Mr. Mayor, that it will
not inconvenience them.

449
00:31:51,117 --> 00:31:52,160
Of course.

450
00:31:54,120 --> 00:31:55,830
You have my word.

451
00:31:56,748 --> 00:32:00,752
[sinister music playing]

452
00:32:11,012 --> 00:32:12,013
-[tearing check]
-Here.

453
00:32:12,096 --> 00:32:14,098
[sinister music playing]

454
00:32:21,105 --> 00:32:21,898
TWENTY-FIVE MILLION PESOS ONLY

455
00:32:24,400 --> 00:32:28,237
I want to host a fundraising
dinner for the congressman.

456
00:32:28,905 --> 00:32:29,906
Fundraiser?

457
00:32:33,743 --> 00:32:36,746
I just thought that, since
I've invested a huge amount

458
00:32:36,829 --> 00:32:38,790
on the export processing zone,

459
00:32:40,792 --> 00:32:44,003
I want to make sure the
Ardientes will keep it running.

460
00:32:44,504 --> 00:32:47,924
So, I might as well go all the way.

461
00:32:50,802 --> 00:32:51,970
For our success.

462
00:32:52,053 --> 00:32:55,515
[sinister music continues playing]

463
00:33:15,410 --> 00:33:19,747
["Sa'Yo" instrumental playing]

464
00:33:42,186 --> 00:33:43,187
[sighs]

465
00:33:44,147 --> 00:33:45,148
Arnaldo!

466
00:33:47,191 --> 00:33:49,652
Who gave you the right
to take the cooperative's lot?

467
00:33:50,111 --> 00:33:51,571
You're heartless!

468
00:33:54,282 --> 00:33:55,783
Calm down, bro.

469
00:33:57,243 --> 00:33:58,161
You know…

470
00:34:01,622 --> 00:34:04,709
No one's taking anything.

471
00:34:05,501 --> 00:34:08,212
In fact, you should thank me.

472
00:34:09,630 --> 00:34:13,134
Because those peasants will be
compensated appropriately.

473
00:34:15,762 --> 00:34:16,763
I did it for them.

474
00:34:17,305 --> 00:34:20,016
For Poblacion Ardiente!

475
00:34:22,018 --> 00:34:23,895
Hold on. Why are you so angry?

476
00:34:25,897 --> 00:34:28,399
They aren't complaining.

477
00:34:31,778 --> 00:34:32,820
Relax, Diego.

478
00:34:33,780 --> 00:34:35,073
Stress is bad for the heart.

479
00:34:39,702 --> 00:34:41,871
[Arnaldo whistles]

480
00:34:48,795 --> 00:34:51,839
[suspenseful music playing]

481
00:34:54,008 --> 00:34:55,593
-Tonyo.
-[cocks gun]

482
00:34:58,805 --> 00:34:59,806
I need some information.

483
00:35:01,599 --> 00:35:04,102
[Camia] <i>Please stay away from me!</i>

484
00:35:04,185 --> 00:35:06,896
<i>Please… Go away!</i>

485
00:35:07,563 --> 00:35:10,233
<i>Lily… Run!</i>

486
00:35:10,316 --> 00:35:11,442
<i>Shut up!</i>

487
00:35:13,444 --> 00:35:14,695
<i>-No!</i>
-[gunshot]

488
00:35:32,672 --> 00:35:38,177
[phone ringing]

489
00:35:39,011 --> 00:35:39,846
Jepoy?

490
00:35:39,929 --> 00:35:42,598
Ivy, I know where they buried your mother.

491
00:35:46,769 --> 00:35:48,813
You do? Where?

492
00:35:49,438 --> 00:35:51,023
Jepoy, where are you? I'm going there!

493
00:35:51,566 --> 00:35:52,775
Don't. Stay there.

494
00:35:54,360 --> 00:35:55,903
You still have to meet the Ardientes.

495
00:35:55,987 --> 00:35:58,156
No, Jepoy. I'll go there!

496
00:35:58,239 --> 00:36:00,449
I don't care about the
Ardientes! Where are you?!

497
00:36:01,159 --> 00:36:01,909
Ivy.

498
00:36:02,952 --> 00:36:05,830
You have to face them or
your plans will be ruined.

499
00:36:09,792 --> 00:36:12,295
Bring me my mother. Bring her back home.

500
00:36:14,255 --> 00:36:15,798
<i>Bring her here.</i>

501
00:36:15,882 --> 00:36:17,425
Bring her back to me.

502
00:36:41,574 --> 00:36:43,784
Diego, why aren't you getting ready yet?

503
00:36:44,202 --> 00:36:45,411
-What?
-Everyone at the market

504
00:36:45,494 --> 00:36:48,831
was talking about the huge
party at Ms. Ivy's mansion.

505
00:36:49,790 --> 00:36:51,334
Aren't you going?

506
00:36:58,341 --> 00:37:01,052
Her invitation was just a formality.

507
00:37:02,136 --> 00:37:03,638
I don't need to be there.

508
00:37:04,180 --> 00:37:06,432
But you should still go.

509
00:37:06,974 --> 00:37:10,937
What if they discuss the cooperative?

510
00:37:11,270 --> 00:37:13,940
Shouldn't at least one of us
be there to hear it?

511
00:37:22,782 --> 00:37:25,701
-Is Dad going to the party?
-Of course!

512
00:37:25,993 --> 00:37:30,289
He won't pass up this chance
to meet prominent people,

513
00:37:30,373 --> 00:37:32,041
including the beautiful girls there.

514
00:37:32,124 --> 00:37:33,542
Your dad wouldn't miss it.

515
00:37:34,961 --> 00:37:36,754
You know how he is.

516
00:37:36,837 --> 00:37:38,381
He dabbles in politics.

517
00:37:38,464 --> 00:37:40,716
And he wants to run
for the local elections.

518
00:37:41,634 --> 00:37:43,094
[exhales]

519
00:37:44,095 --> 00:37:47,556
About Ivy, by the way,
be careful around her.

520
00:37:48,849 --> 00:37:51,936
After she saved your life,
you still have doubts about her.

521
00:37:52,270 --> 00:37:55,022
She's even helping Grandpa,
and she doesn't have to.

522
00:37:56,732 --> 00:37:57,775
-[scoffs]
-And wait a second.

523
00:37:57,858 --> 00:38:01,028
I thought you saw her as family.

524
00:38:02,405 --> 00:38:03,364
Hmm…

525
00:38:03,447 --> 00:38:05,533
That conversation was
supposed to be private.

526
00:38:06,450 --> 00:38:07,785
Why did she mention that?

527
00:38:08,536 --> 00:38:09,829
Son, all I'm saying is…

528
00:38:10,454 --> 00:38:12,540
we don't know her that well.

529
00:38:12,790 --> 00:38:15,793
She's not part of our world.
She's a total stranger!

530
00:38:16,627 --> 00:38:20,047
I'm not sure if she's
showing us her true colors.

531
00:38:20,131 --> 00:38:21,340
That's all I'm worried about.

532
00:38:22,216 --> 00:38:23,718
So… Let's go?

533
00:38:23,801 --> 00:38:25,177
Let's go to the party for your grandpa.

534
00:38:34,228 --> 00:38:37,857
[tense music playing]

535
00:38:48,993 --> 00:38:52,663
[music intensifies]

536
00:39:09,597 --> 00:39:13,768
[subtle music playing]

537
00:39:40,836 --> 00:39:42,963
[sobbing]

538
00:39:50,221 --> 00:39:51,305
Where's my mother?

539
00:39:51,389 --> 00:39:53,974
I told you to bring her to me.

540
00:39:54,809 --> 00:39:56,727
Why didn't you bring her to me?

541
00:39:57,686 --> 00:39:58,938
She's in a safe place.

542
00:39:59,855 --> 00:40:01,023
I can't bring her body here.

543
00:40:01,107 --> 00:40:02,817
It's too risky.

544
00:40:04,443 --> 00:40:06,529
-Ivy…
-[Ivy weeps]

545
00:40:06,862 --> 00:40:08,489
Ivy, calm down.

546
00:40:09,365 --> 00:40:11,784
You can't let the Ardientes
suspect anything.

547
00:40:13,702 --> 00:40:15,079
The Ardientes?

548
00:40:16,789 --> 00:40:18,749
They're monsters.

549
00:40:20,418 --> 00:40:21,585
That mayor…

550
00:40:24,505 --> 00:40:25,631
the governor…

551
00:40:27,758 --> 00:40:29,009
and the congressman.

552
00:40:30,511 --> 00:40:34,723
I'll take them all down one by one.

553
00:40:34,807 --> 00:40:37,518
All of them. All the Ardientes!

554
00:40:38,936 --> 00:40:40,187
They'll pay.

555
00:40:40,271 --> 00:40:42,857
[Carlotta] Ivy? Sweetie.

556
00:40:44,525 --> 00:40:45,860
The Ardientes are here.

557
00:41:17,975 --> 00:41:20,853
[sinister music playing]

558
00:41:36,577 --> 00:41:39,580
-[jazz music playing]
-[indistinct chatter]

559
00:41:57,640 --> 00:42:01,769
Stop being so obvious
about wanting this house.

560
00:42:02,228 --> 00:42:03,479
It's going to be ours.

561
00:42:04,813 --> 00:42:06,398
We'll use her.

562
00:42:08,067 --> 00:42:09,777
And bleed her dry.

563
00:42:10,986 --> 00:42:15,199
Just like the last owner of this house.

564
00:42:21,664 --> 00:42:24,375
[Natalie] Arnaldo. Hi.

565
00:42:25,960 --> 00:42:27,253
-Hi, Auntie.
-Hello.

566
00:42:27,336 --> 00:42:30,381
Hello. Hello.

567
00:42:30,464 --> 00:42:31,257
-Hi.
-Good evening.

568
00:42:31,340 --> 00:42:32,132
Good evening.

569
00:42:32,216 --> 00:42:33,050
Good evening, Uncle.

570
00:42:36,178 --> 00:42:38,889
[Natalie] What an amazing house.

571
00:42:39,431 --> 00:42:41,308
Ivy's house is beautiful.

572
00:42:44,270 --> 00:42:45,771
Is Diego coming?

573
00:42:47,690 --> 00:42:49,400
I don't know where he is.

574
00:42:50,442 --> 00:42:51,277
[woman] Ladies and gentlemen,

575
00:42:51,360 --> 00:42:52,903
may I have your attention, please?

576
00:42:53,153 --> 00:42:55,739
Ms. Ivy Aguas is on her way down.

577
00:42:56,615 --> 00:42:57,575
Please.

578
00:43:13,424 --> 00:43:17,428
[tense music playing]

579
00:43:45,789 --> 00:43:49,793
[tense music continues playing]

580
00:44:02,806 --> 00:44:06,810
[sinister music playing]

581
00:44:10,939 --> 00:44:14,943
[guests clapping]

582
00:44:27,081 --> 00:44:28,290
[music intensifies]

583
00:44:32,419 --> 00:44:36,131
<i>I want you to remember my face.</i>

584
00:44:38,717 --> 00:44:40,177
<i>I'll bring you down one by one</i>

585
00:44:40,260 --> 00:44:42,304
<i>till you're begging for mercy…</i>

586
00:44:42,846 --> 00:44:45,057
<i>and the sweet reprise of death.</i>

587
00:44:48,519 --> 00:44:51,647
<i>Just like how you murdered my family.</i>

588
00:44:52,189 --> 00:44:55,401
<i>Just like how my mother begged for mercy.</i>

589
00:45:05,953 --> 00:45:09,289
<i>I am Ivy Aguas.</i>

590
00:45:14,795 --> 00:45:17,047
<i>And I am vengeance.</i>

591
00:45:17,423 --> 00:45:21,427
[sinister music playing]

592
00:45:39,528 --> 00:45:43,532
[sinister music playing]

593
00:45:57,296 --> 00:46:00,132
<i>Sometimes, it's so hard being honest.</i>

594
00:46:00,215 --> 00:46:01,341
[Ivy] <i>You're right, Governor.</i>

595
00:46:01,425 --> 00:46:04,386
<i>Like with men. They cheat so blatantly.</i>

596
00:46:05,179 --> 00:46:09,183
<i>My boyfriend is not a book nor is he a toy</i>

597
00:46:09,266 --> 00:46:10,767
<i>that can be borrowed or shared.</i>

598
00:46:10,851 --> 00:46:12,144
[Ivy] <i>You can have Arnaldo.</i>

599
00:46:12,227 --> 00:46:15,314
<i>I like my toys brand new.</i>

600
00:46:16,940 --> 00:46:18,025
-[screams]
-[objects shatter]

601
00:46:18,108 --> 00:46:18,901
[Diego] <i>Ma.</i>

602
00:46:18,984 --> 00:46:20,819
<i>You've got the skin</i>
<i>of a crocodile, Governor.</i>

603
00:46:20,903 --> 00:46:22,070
[Emilia] <i>I shall see you tomorrow.</i>

604
00:46:22,154 --> 00:46:25,407
<i>And don't worry, my maids</i>
<i>won't spill coffee on you.</i>

605
00:46:25,616 --> 00:46:28,827
[Ivy] <i>I invested a lot. That</i>
<i>means I'll reap something bigger</i>

606
00:46:28,911 --> 00:46:29,995
<i>in return.</i>

607
00:46:30,162 --> 00:46:32,748
[theme music playing]
